{"files":[{"content":"/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <sys/time.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\n\n// matrix to be solved\ndouble **grid;\n\n// auxiliary matrix\ndouble **new_grid;\n\n// size of each side of the grid\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\n// return the absolute value of a number\ndouble absolute(double num){\n    if(num < 0)\n        return -1.0 * num;\n    return num;\n}\n\n\n// allocate memory for the grid\nvoid allocate_memory(){\n    grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n        new_grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n    }\n}\n\n// initialize both buffers identically so untouched border cells remain valid after swaps\nvoid initialize_grid(){\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup){\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\n                new_grid[i][j] = 100;\n            } else {\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\n                new_grid[i][j] = 0.0;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// save the grid in a file\nvoid save_grid(){\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", grid[i][j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\n\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n    \n    int hasError = 1;\n    int iter = 0;\n\n    struct timeval time_start;\n    struct timeval time_end;\n\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\n    allocate_memory();\n\n    // set grid initial conditions\n    initialize_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\n\", size, size);\n\n    // get the start time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\n\n    // Jacobi iteration\n    // This loop will end if either the maximum change reaches below a set threshold (convergence)\n    // or a fixed number of maximum iterations have completed\n    while ( hasError && iter < iter_max_num ) {\n\n        hasError = 0;\n        // calculates the Laplace equation to determine each cell's next value\n        for( int i = 1; i < size-1; i++) {\n            for(int j = 1; j < size-1; j++) {\n\n                new_grid[i][j] = 0.25 * (grid[i][j+1] + grid[i][j-1] +\n                                         grid[i-1][j] + grid[i+1][j]);\n\n                double errorCurrent = absolute(new_grid[i][j] - grid[i][j]);\n                if(errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD ){\n                    hasError = 1;                                        \n                }     \n            }\n        }\n\n        // Swap buffers instead of copying every interior cell.\n        double **tmp = grid;\n        grid = new_grid;\n        new_grid = tmp;\n        iter++;\n    }\n\n    // get the end time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\n\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\n\n    //save the final grid in file\n    save_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\n\", exec_time, iter);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/laplace_seq.c"}],"hypothesis":"Replacing the per-sweep interior copy with a ping-pong buffer swap should reduce memory traffic in the Jacobi iteration while preserving its output and convergence behavior.","notes":"Both buffers are initialized identically, including borders, so swaps preserve the original boundary values even for small valid grids. The stencil expression, error test, iteration limit, and printed active buffer are unchanged. No commands were run.","sources_kept":[], "transformations":["Initialize both buffers to the same initial grid, including untouched border cells.","Remove the interior copy pass and swap the buffer pointers after each executed sweep, including the sweep that triggers convergence."]}